<article class="env-lemma" id="0C0M">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C0M">Lemma <span data-tag="0C0M">58.16.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a proper morphism with geometrically connected fibres. Let $s' \leadsto s$ be a specialization of points of $S$ and let $sp : \pi _1(X_{\overline{s}'}) \to \pi _1(X_{\overline{s}})$ be a specialization map. Then there exists a strictly henselian valuation ring $R$ over $S$ with algebraically closed fraction field such that $sp$ is isomorphic to $sp_ R$ defined above. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{O}_{S, s} \to A$ be the strict henselization constructed using $\kappa (s) \to \kappa (\overline{s})$. Let $A \to \kappa (\overline{s}')$ be the map used to construct $sp$. Let $R \subset \kappa (\overline{s}')$ be a valuation ring with fraction field $\kappa (\overline{s}')$ dominating the image of $A$. See Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00IA" data-tag="00IA">10.50.2</a>. Observe that $R$ is strictly henselian for example by Lemma <a href="/tag/0BSQ" data-tag="0BSQ">58.12.2</a> and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00IC" data-tag="00IC">10.50.3</a>. Then the lemma is clear. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>